This repository is distributed under two licenses. Which one applies is decided
by the file, not by the package: a single npm tarball carries both.

  SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0 AND UPL-1.0

REUSE.toml is the machine-readable form of the table below and the authority
when the two disagree.


The server: MPL-2.0
-------------------

  src/            the MCP server, its parsers, indexes and tests
  bin/            the launcher and the type stripper
  scripts/        the gates and the commit signer
  .github/        the CI checks
  eval/           the agentic eval fixture
  docs/design/    how the server is put together
  docs/plans/     how a scope was scoped
  docs/evals/     what the eval measured
  dist/           the build of src/, when one exists
  tsconfig.json, package.json, package-lock.json

Full text in LICENSES/MPL-2.0.txt.

MPL-2.0 applies file by file. A distributed copy keeps these files, with any
changes to them, under MPL-2.0 and open source. Files added beside them can
have any license.


The corpus: UPL-1.0
-------------------

  bugs/                          repros for what is broken in the pinned nightly
  corpus/language/               Builtin.roc, langref/ and
                                 examples/all_roc_syntax.roc mirrored from
                                 roc-lang/roc; langref/local/, overview/ and
                                 topics/ ours
  corpus/platforms/              each platform release's examples and
                                 signature index (index.json), and our
                                 overviews, topics and scaffolds written
                                 against them
  corpus/packages/               each package release's signature index
                                 (index.json), and our overviews and topics
  README.md, CLA.md, plugins/README.md, the UPSTREAM files

Full text in LICENSES/UPL-1.0.txt. Upstream copyright lines, releases and
provenance are in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

The corpus is permissive on purpose. An agent reads these files and reproduces
what it finds into somebody's application, and no snippet an agent hands you
should arrive carrying an obligation. UPL is also what the Roc ecosystem uses,
which is what every tree mirrored here was already published under.


Commercial use
--------------

This project aims to help grow the Roc community. Commercial use is permitted.
Using, modifying and hosting the server carry no obligations. Obligations
attach only when you distribute copies, and only to the server's own files.

Using the server does not license what you write with it. The corpus is UPL-1.0,
so a snippet an agent lifts out of a topic file carries nothing into your
codebase.

  Closed-source, commercial or client work         None
  Shipping what an agent wrote with its help       None. The output is yours
  Team-wide installs, CI                           None
  Modifying it for internal use                    None. Internal use is not
                                                   distribution
  Hosting it, modified or not                      None. Hosting is not
                                                   distribution
  Paid consulting, training, support or services   None
  Redistributing it unmodified, in an image or     Keep the copyright notices,
  an internal mirror                               and pass on LICENSE and
                                                   LICENSES/
  Distributing a modified copy                     The same, and make the
                                                   source of the server files
                                                   you changed available under
                                                   MPL-2.0
  Shipping it inside a larger closed-source        The same. Your own files
  product                                          stay closed
  Publishing a plugin under any license,           None. A plugin is a separate
  including for your own commercial platform       package, not a derivative.
                                                   What it vendors carries its
                                                   own license

Not permitted: distributing the server's own files without their source, or
under terms that remove MPL-2.0 from them, and removing the copyright notices.


plugins/
--------

Each directory under plugins/ is a separate npm package with its own license.
None is part of this package: the `files` list in package.json does not name
plugins/. See plugins/roc-ray/LICENSE (UPL-1.0), plugins/joy/LICENSE
(Apache-2.0), and plugins/weaver/LICENSE, which says which of its files are
UPL-1.0 and which are upstream's, for which upstream states no license yet.
